        <groundspeak:log id="682496605">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-30T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="12442378">mikefromcanmore</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP303 Millet.  As noted getting to and touching the cap isn't a problem getting a picture is another story.  We finally had a warm day and mud everywhere but luckily still no bugs.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682015383">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6887855">JREnarson</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP303 - Millet&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our first of two brass caps for the day.  However, we weren't totally able to log this one.  Arriving at GZ, the location of the brass cap was found with no problem.  However, it was located at the bottom of a hole in a ditch that had a lot of standing water in it all over the place.  &quot;J&quot; reached down to find the brass cap, and found it over 6&quot; below ground level (i.e. 6+ inches below water level).  So it was impossible to read what was written on the cap.  Still calling this as a Find though, as we located the cap and did the best we could to read the unreadable writing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks again OFTH for all of your work in maintaining this virtual cache for so many years.  It will be sad to see this one go.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680657950">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-21T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="13954990">0728ALH</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;Bcp303 Millet&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Team Pixos, 97CMA, 0728ALH, make a great team finding Brass Caps or even caches in general.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today saw us finding 14 caps. The biggest day for us for cap finds ever.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We really do enjoy where the caps take us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the caps.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
